  "documentation": {
	"summary": "Sine Space: a stationary contact surface and a moving visible passage",
	"layout": "20x48 m. The corridor ends before a 14x24 m open basin. Three-metre full-width ramps descend to the stationary sine relief at -1m and climb back to a six-metre exit landing. The relief spans z21..39; solid side walls prevent a flat bypass. Colour rain remains.",
	"objective": "Predict a sphere departure, release, change only body size or relief, then compare the colliding tray with the corridor walls that permit crossing. Keep the counter and the measured x-gap explicit.",
	"key_elements": [
	  "All six authored exhibits retained: tray, wall explanation, corridor, sine terrain, dark sphere and colour rain.",
	  "Basin x2..16,z18..42; bottom -2.2m. No fire or glass lid.",
	  "Terrain at (9,30), rim -1m; rain at (9,29), same height relative to terrain.",
	  "Broad entry ramp z18..21; exit ramp z39..42. Clear landing before the onward door at (9,45).",
	  "The earlier tutorial code remains unchanged; this is museum access geometry.",
      "Ramp toes continue underneath the relief, below its lowest trough, to avoid an exposed collision edge at the join."
	]
  },
